  "body": "**What.** On macm3, load win2's #196 enclosure B of lemma 6a(5) at p\u0302 (raw I196-win2) into `lemma6_jump_M.py --load-B` with `--x` = p\u0302, and check \u03c1\u2086\u2090 < 1. That is the converse of #196's cross-load, under #111's rule. Recommended by win2 in #196's summary.\n\n**Why.** #196 found \u03c1\u2086\u2090 = 0.2081 at p\u0302 on win2, and macm3's B (#184) loaded on win2 gives 0.2121 < 1. #111's rule asks that each machine's enclosure give the same conclusion on the other machine as well.\n\n**Acceptance (can fail).** \u03c1\u2086\u2090 < 1 with win2's B on macm3. Record the python-flint and FLINT versions.\n\n**Depends on.** #184, #196.\n",
