   "body": "## Summary (macm3, 06:30 UTC)\n\n**Result.** win2's enclosure B of lemma 6a(5) at p\u0302 (I196-win2), loaded on macm3 with `--x` = p\u0302, gives **\u03c1\u2086\u2090 = [0.2081327461 \u00b1 2.72e-11] < 1**. #111's rule is met in both directions: each machine's B gives \u03c1\u2086\u2090 < 1 on the other (macm3's B on win2: 0.2121 in #196).\n\n| item | result |\n|---|---|\n| \u03c1\u2086\u2090 with win2's B on macm3 | **[0.2081327461 \u00b1 2.72e-11] < 1**, ok true, |H| \u2264 63.9, |G_slow\u207b\u00b9| \u2264 5.16, max radius of B 3.21e-05 |\n| win2's own B on win2 (I196) | [0.2081327454 \u00b1 8.77e-12] |\n| macm3's own B on macm3 (#184) / on win2 (I196) | [0.2120798569 \u00b1 1.46e-11] / [0.2120798570 \u00b1 2.97e-11] |\n| python-flint and FLINT | python-flint 0.9.0, FLINT 3.6.0 (Python 3.14.3; win2 3.14.10, same pins) |\n\n**Run.** `lemma6_jump_M.py --M=5 --box=I103-macm3/A_M2_6a_M5_sub1e-18.json --x=$PHAT --rp=0.08 --k=20 --load-B=I196-win2/B_M5_sub1e-18_phat.json`, $PHAT the six decimal strings of the box file's `p` (`centre_passed.txt`, `diff`-equal to `p`; the script prints no centre line, as in #184). 16 s for all steps, awake. main d28566c0.\n\n**The balls differ and the conclusion does not.** The \u03c1\u2086\u2090 ball of this cross-load and win2's own ball of the same B are disjoint by 6.4e-10 (their difference 7e-10, the radii 2.7e-11 and 8.8e-12): the stored radii are rounded to a 30-bit mag on reload and the enclosures' radii depend on the integration path (#104, #110), the situation #111's rule exists for. macm3's own B and its reload on win2 overlap. Both conclusions are \u03c1\u2086\u2090 < 1.\n\n**Controls (my addition, with win2's B).** `--mutate=partial` exit 0 (G_slow 13 \u00d7 17, not square, \"failure expected\"), `--mutate=coords` exit 2 with \u03c1\u2086\u2090 = 3.200 (not below 1), `review_39/b_float.py` exit 0 with the flow at p\u0302 within **4.64e-08** of rad(B) (limit 0.01; the flow from x\u0302 is at 0.184), and its `--mutate=w` exit 0 (232 of rad(B), must exceed 1).\n\n**Acceptance.** \u03c1\u2086\u2090 < 1 with win2's B on macm3: met. Versions recorded: met.\n\n**Discrepancies.** None.\n\n**Raw.** `I220-macm3/` of the raw-data repository, commit 4fc94ee (the logs, the JSON, exits.txt, versions.txt, centre_passed.txt, run_i220.sh, README). `raw_check.py` exits 0.\n\n### Recommended tasks\n\nNone.\n",
